  "question": {
    "text": "Consider two concentric spherical metal shells of radii $r_{1}$ and $r_{2}\\left(r_{2}>r_{1}\\right)$. If the outer shell has a charge $q$ and the inner one is grounded, the charge on the inner shell is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vSwWC",
      "text": "$\\frac{-r_{2}}{5}, q$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "I3skS",
      "text": "zero",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RoBAZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{-r_{1}}{r_{2}} q$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MaVmk",
      "text": "$-q$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, the charge on the inner shell be $q^{\\prime}$\r\nThe total charge will be zero\r\nSo, $\\frac{k q^{\\prime}}{r_{1}}+\\frac{k q}{r_{2}}=0$\r\n$\\left(\\because r_{2}>r_{1}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad q^{\\prime}=-\\frac{K q / r_{2}}{K / r_{1}}$\r\n$$\r\nq^{\\prime}=-\\left(\\frac{r_{1}}{r_{2}}\\right) q\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
